WEBVTT

1
00:02:13.922 --> 00:02:18.922
That is quite low. Yes, that is quite good.

2
00:02:21.922 --> 00:02:29.922
In Open Church, we teach for a month every November about relationships.

3
00:02:29.922 --> 00:02:39.922
And what I mean by relationships is not just dating, not just marriage, but also, for example, collegiality.

4
00:02:39.922 --> 00:02:44.922
It is also how we interact with each other in this society.

5
00:02:44.922 --> 00:02:52.922
Relationships also include what your relationship is to your neighbor who is not in Christ. How do you deal with that?

6
00:02:52.922 --> 00:02:56.922
Relationships also encompass how you interact with your family.

7
00:02:56.922 --> 00:03:08.922
These are social, societal, psychological, emotional, and especially spiritual relationships that I want to talk about every November.

8
00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:12.922
And we call that being open about relationships.

9
00:03:12.922 --> 00:03:18.922
You will see me twice. Three times, four times, five times, six times.

10
00:03:18.922 --> 00:03:23.922
I don't know if you can handle that. I don't know if you can handle that.

11
00:03:23.922 --> 00:03:31.922
The beauty might be too much for you. If that is the case, enjoy the ride.

12
00:03:32.922 --> 00:03:36.922
Wow, do I look like this?

13
00:03:36.922 --> 00:03:40.922
I find this month very important.

14
00:03:40.922 --> 00:03:50.922
Because in open church, in the church, when we do not speak about marriage and we neglect that, we forget it.

15
00:03:50.922 --> 00:03:55.922
Because there are, of course, millions of topics.

16
00:03:55.922 --> 00:03:58.922
God's Word is indeed everlasting.

17
00:03:58.922 --> 00:04:01.922
You can read every book on earth.

18
00:04:01.922 --> 00:04:06.922
And after reading that book once or twice or at most three times, you have probably read it enough.

19
00:04:06.922 --> 00:04:08.922
But not so with God's Word.

20
00:04:08.922 --> 00:04:11.922
God's Word is a stream of living water.

21
00:04:11.922 --> 00:04:13.922
And it just keeps going, and it just keeps going.

22
00:04:13.922 --> 00:04:16.922
For it is not information, it is revelation.

23
00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:19.922
God's Word keeps going.

24
00:04:19.922 --> 00:04:23.922
You can chew on John 3 verse 16 for the rest of your life.

25
00:04:23.922 --> 00:04:27.922
And this is such a beautiful verse because it is a living word.

26
00:04:27.922 --> 00:04:30.922
God's Word is alive. Hallelujah.

27
00:04:30.922 --> 00:04:37.922
And so we can talk about so many subjects that are important.

28
00:04:37.922 --> 00:04:44.922
But I find it important, also as a church, that we pause annually as a sort of curriculum.

29
00:04:44.922 --> 00:04:51.922
That we repeat things and that we keep hammering on certain pillar matters of our faith.

30
00:04:51.922 --> 00:04:57.922
And one of those is how we arrange our relationships or how we interact with each other and such matters.

31
00:04:57.922 --> 00:05:02.922
So marriage is very important to teach regularly.

32
00:05:02.922 --> 00:05:06.922
For some people who have been married for a long time and have been in Christ for a long time,

33
00:05:06.922 --> 00:05:09.922
this is basic information.

34
00:05:09.922 --> 00:05:11.922
And then you think to yourself, well, doesn't everyone understand that?

35
00:05:11.922 --> 00:05:13.922
But that is not the case.

36
00:05:13.922 --> 00:05:17.922
For if society, if the world no longer believes in Jesus,

37
00:05:17.922 --> 00:05:20.922
then the world of Christianity will revert to paganism.

38
00:05:20.922 --> 00:05:27.922
And if you live in paganism, then people do not know how to handle relationships in the name of Jesus.

39
00:05:27.922 --> 00:05:29.922
People do not know at all what a marriage is.

40
00:05:29.922 --> 00:05:32.922
People do not know at all how to deal with sex.

41
00:05:32.922 --> 00:05:36.922
People do not know how to be forgiving towards each other at all.

42
00:05:36.922 --> 00:05:39.922
For this is not what paganism teaches.

43
00:05:39.922 --> 00:05:45.922
And therefore it is important in Christianity, in our faith in Jesus Christ,

44
00:05:45.922 --> 00:05:49.922
to continue to teach how we approach these basic principles.

45
00:05:49.922 --> 00:05:56.922
Today, and this whole month, I want to talk about the topic Free Indeed.

46
00:05:56.922 --> 00:06:02.922
And that comes from the Bible verse where Jesus says in John 8, verse 36,

47
00:06:02.922 --> 00:06:06.922
Only when the Son has set you free, are you truly free.

48
00:06:06.922 --> 00:06:11.922
Only when Jesus sets you free, are you truly free.

49
00:06:11.922 --> 00:06:14.922
Everything else is false freedom.

50
00:06:14.922 --> 00:06:21.922
The world, as they sometimes call themselves liberal or free, is not free.

51
00:06:21.922 --> 00:06:28.922
It is not freedom to live outside of Christ, for you are as trapped as can be.

52
00:06:28.922 --> 00:06:34.922
Well, one of the things, I don't want to go on too long about my own testimony,

53
00:06:34.922 --> 00:06:37.922
but I will address it for a minute or so.

54
00:06:37.922 --> 00:06:44.922
One of the things I needed freedom from as a person was in the area of addictions.

55
00:06:44.922 --> 00:06:46.922
And we will talk about that this whole month.

56
00:06:46.922 --> 00:06:54.922
Addictions are things that hold you back from actually being able to function in life.

57
00:06:54.922 --> 00:06:57.922
To function freely, truly free.

58
00:06:57.922 --> 00:07:01.922
And to truly worship God freely.

59
00:07:01.922 --> 00:07:03.922
For what is freedom?

60
00:07:03.922 --> 00:07:07.922
Freedom is to be in the presence of the Son.

61
00:07:07.922 --> 00:07:09.922
That is true freedom.

62
00:07:09.922 --> 00:07:13.922
Everything else is nonsense. Hallelujah.

63
00:07:13.922 --> 00:07:15.922
And so this month I call Free Indeed.

64
00:07:15.922 --> 00:07:25.922
And this month I will explain basic principles about breaking free from addictions, as I once learned them.

65
00:07:25.922 --> 00:07:30.922
When I grew up in a Christian family with two wonderful parents,

66
00:07:30.922 --> 00:07:36.922
I experienced things in my life that ultimately led me to make choices,

67
00:07:36.922 --> 00:07:41.922
which ultimately led me to develop addictions in my life.

68
00:07:41.922 --> 00:07:45.922
I went out a lot. I worked hard. I worked hard in construction.

69
00:07:45.922 --> 00:07:48.922
I hated every day on the construction site. I don't understand what people do in construction.

70
00:07:48.922 --> 00:07:51.922
But I did it. I just did it.

71
00:07:51.922 --> 00:07:53.922
Forty, fifty hours a week I was on the construction site.

72
00:07:53.922 --> 00:07:56.922
Working hard. Also picking up extra work on Saturdays.

73
00:07:56.922 --> 00:08:01.922
But as soon as the weekend came, I started on pills, coke, ketamine, GHB.

74
00:08:01.922 --> 00:08:05.922
I took everything I could get my hands on. And I took a lot of it.

75
00:08:05.922 --> 00:08:09.922
And I took so much because I just wanted to black out.

76
00:08:09.922 --> 00:08:11.922
I wanted to party all weekend long.

77
00:08:11.922 --> 00:08:15.922
During the week I didn't use anything. I wasn't a heroin junkie, but I was a face junkie.

78
00:08:15.922 --> 00:08:19.922
And so addiction was one of my big problems.

79
00:08:19.922 --> 00:08:22.922
But through the name of Jesus, I am free.

80
00:08:22.922 --> 00:08:27.922
I am completely free. I don't use coke, just to be clear.

81
00:08:27.922 --> 00:08:29.922
I am completely free.

82
00:08:29.922 --> 00:08:35.922
How long ago is 2008? It is now 2024. Let's say 16 years.

83
00:08:35.922 --> 00:08:38.922
I have been free for 16 years in the name of Jesus.

84
00:08:43.922 --> 00:08:49.922
And I am so happy about that, because through that freedom I have...

85
00:08:49.922 --> 00:08:52.922
And I have been set free by Jesus.

86
00:08:52.922 --> 00:08:55.922
And through that freedom, I met a wonderful woman.

87
00:08:55.922 --> 00:09:00.922
That woman would never have married me if I had been that person from back then.

88
00:09:00.922 --> 00:09:01.922
No way.

89
00:09:01.922 --> 00:09:05.922
Dear people in the audience, speaking openly about relationships.

90
00:09:05.922 --> 00:09:12.922
Ladies, don't get involved with that tough guy who is still stuck in addiction.

91
00:09:12.922 --> 00:09:14.922
Don't do it.

92
00:09:14.922 --> 00:09:17.922
He can be as handsome as I don't know what.

93
00:09:17.922 --> 00:09:20.922
He can have as much money as I don't know what.

94
00:09:20.922 --> 00:09:22.922
He can speak beautifully as I don't know what.

95
00:09:22.922 --> 00:09:26.922
But if he is clearly stuck in addiction, don't go there.

96
00:09:26.922 --> 00:09:35.922
Because the fact that I am free from addiction is that I was able to marry this beautiful woman.

97
00:09:35.922 --> 00:09:40.922
But I am sure she would not have wanted anything to do with me if she had known that person from back then.

98
00:09:41.922 --> 00:09:43.922
At one point, we were driving home.

99
00:09:43.922 --> 00:09:46.922
I am boasting a bit about myself now, but I am allowed to.

100
00:09:46.922 --> 00:09:50.922
At one point, we were driving home after a Christmas party.

101
00:09:50.922 --> 00:09:53.922
We drove home and I always drive.

102
00:09:53.922 --> 00:09:55.922
I am always the designated driver.

103
00:09:55.922 --> 00:09:57.922
I am never drunk, I don't do that.

104
00:09:57.922 --> 00:10:03.922
And Vanessa said to me, honey, I'm so proud of you.

105
00:10:03.922 --> 00:10:06.922
Because I've never seen you under influence.

106
00:10:07.922 --> 00:10:14.922
As long as I've known Vanessa, we have been married for almost thirteen years, but Vanessa has never seen me under influence.

107
00:10:14.922 --> 00:10:16.922
And I want to keep it that way.

108
00:10:16.922 --> 00:10:19.922
And I want to raise my children so that they have never seen daddy drunk.

109
00:10:19.922 --> 00:10:22.922
And that they have never seen daddy high.

110
00:10:22.922 --> 00:10:26.922
Because by the way, we are going to talk about that in week four.

111
00:10:26.922 --> 00:10:30.922
Being free from addiction as a responsibility in the family.

112
00:10:30.922 --> 00:10:33.922
But today I want to, oh yes, now I'm going to say this.

113
00:10:33.922 --> 00:10:40.922
So I came in 2008, in 2007, I said to that Lord.

114
00:10:40.922 --> 00:10:44.922
Lord, I am so sick and tired of my own life.

115
00:10:44.922 --> 00:10:49.922
I am so sick of it to know Jesus.

116
00:10:49.922 --> 00:10:51.922
To love Jesus.

117
00:10:51.922 --> 00:10:54.922
But almost every evening having to say sorry to God.

118
00:10:54.922 --> 00:10:58.922
I don't know if you can relate, but I had a very long time a relationship with God.

119
00:10:58.922 --> 00:11:02.922
That my prayer didn't go much further than asking for forgiveness every day again.

120
00:11:02.922 --> 00:11:04.922
Oh Lord, I've messed up again.

121
00:11:04.922 --> 00:11:05.922
Oh Lord, I have done wrong again.

122
00:11:05.922 --> 00:11:06.922
Create in me a clean heart.

123
00:11:06.922 --> 00:11:08.922
Renew a right spirit in me.

124
00:11:08.922 --> 00:11:09.922
Cast me not away, bla, bla, bla.

125
00:11:09.922 --> 00:11:11.922
And then again, the next day watched porn again.

126
00:11:11.922 --> 00:11:13.922
And the next day got high again.

127
00:11:13.922 --> 00:11:14.922
And the next day again.

128
00:11:14.922 --> 00:11:15.922
Every time doing wrong again.

129
00:11:15.922 --> 00:11:18.922
And trying, and trying, and trying.

130
00:11:18.922 --> 00:11:21.922
At one point even trying to give myself in the church.

131
00:11:21.922 --> 00:11:22.922
Playing along.

132
00:11:22.922 --> 00:11:23.922
I played piano.

133
00:11:23.922 --> 00:11:24.922
Yes, I played piano very well.

134
00:11:24.922 --> 00:11:30.922
And I played piano, but sometimes I was still just high or still just drunk from the night before.

135
00:11:30.922 --> 00:11:34.922
And I was just eating mints to hide behind my own addictions.

136
00:11:34.922 --> 00:11:37.922
And I was so sick and tired of myself.

137
00:11:37.922 --> 00:11:42.922
That I said, Lord, if you want me to live for you as a Son of God.

138
00:11:42.922 --> 00:11:46.922
If you want me to become a man of God, then you must send me away.

139
00:11:46.922 --> 00:11:48.922
For I cannot stay here.

140
00:11:48.922 --> 00:11:51.922
For where I live here is too much fire around me.

141
00:11:51.922 --> 00:11:55.922
And where I live here is too much influence around me.

142
00:11:55.922 --> 00:11:57.922
That pulls me back to that hell every time.

143
00:11:57.922 --> 00:11:58.922
I can't do this.

144
00:11:58.922 --> 00:12:00.922
Lord, you must take me away from here.

145
00:12:00.922 --> 00:12:02.922
Send me literal prayers.

146
00:12:02.922 --> 00:12:08.922
Lord, if you want me to live for you, then you must take me away from here to the other side of the world.

147
00:12:08.922 --> 00:12:09.922
I am not lying.

148
00:12:09.922 --> 00:12:10.922
I am not exaggerating.

149
00:12:10.922 --> 00:12:14.922
That same month, David Reedy came to Rehoboth.

150
00:12:14.922 --> 00:12:18.922
David Reedy was a pastor at Hillsong Church, Sydney.

151
00:12:18.922 --> 00:12:21.922
And he said, Lord, I believe that the Lord has a word for you.

152
00:12:21.922 --> 00:12:24.922
He invites you to go to Australia Bible College.

153
00:12:24.922 --> 00:12:26.922
I had literally prayed this.

154
00:12:26.922 --> 00:12:31.922
Lord, set me free and bring me to the other side of the world, so that I can prepare to live for you.

155
00:12:31.922 --> 00:12:35.922
God has set me free by setting me free in Sydney, Australia.

156
00:12:35.922 --> 00:12:37.922
There I attended Bible College.

157
00:12:37.922 --> 00:12:39.922
There I earned my bachelor's degree.

158
00:12:39.922 --> 00:12:41.922
So I studied there in June.

159
00:12:41.922 --> 00:12:45.922
I studied the Bachelor of Contemporary Ministry there.

160
00:12:45.922 --> 00:12:49.922
So that Contemporary Ministry is, you can study theology there.

161
00:12:49.922 --> 00:12:54.922
But I have a major in theology and a minor in Contemporary Ministry.

162
00:12:54.922 --> 00:12:58.922
So that is actually social work, from a Christian perspective.

163
00:12:58.922 --> 00:13:04.922
And what was so cool is that I actually flew to Sydney, Australia in 2008.

164
00:13:04.922 --> 00:13:09.922
But I was so nervous about going there because I knew this was a milestone in my life.

165
00:13:09.922 --> 00:13:11.922
I knew this was going to clean me up.

166
00:13:11.922 --> 00:13:13.922
I knew this was going to completely change me.

167
00:13:13.922 --> 00:13:15.922
I knew that I had one last chance.

168
00:13:15.922 --> 00:13:17.922
I knew that about myself.

169
00:13:17.922 --> 00:13:22.922
And because I was so nervous about it, the week before I got on the plane,

170
00:13:22.922 --> 00:13:25.922
I completely printed myself off the map.

171
00:13:25.922 --> 00:13:28.922
I was completely off track.

172
00:13:28.922 --> 00:13:30.922
Just completely vague.

173
00:13:30.922 --> 00:13:33.922
Why? Because that addiction was so strong.

174
00:13:33.922 --> 00:13:36.922
And so, why am I saying this?

175
00:13:36.922 --> 00:13:39.922
I went to Australia completely broken.

176
00:13:39.922 --> 00:13:43.922
I was totally broken, I was totally addicted, I was still completely bound.

177
00:13:43.922 --> 00:13:47.922
But I went to Australia with full conviction.

178
00:13:47.922 --> 00:13:52.922
And at one point, I was there in Australia, I wanted to say Openkerk, in Hillsong Church.

179
00:13:52.922 --> 00:13:57.922
And the boss, check this out, the boss of 180TC.

180
00:13:57.922 --> 00:14:02.922
180TC is one of the largest global addiction clinics.

181
00:14:02.922 --> 00:14:06.922
Teen Challenge, David Wilkerson, I don't know if you know him.

182
00:14:06.922 --> 00:14:11.922
Mighty Man of God, who set up Teen Challenge in the sixties and seventies.

183
00:14:11.922 --> 00:14:16.922
A very large rehabilitation clinic, worldwide, everywhere Teen Challenges.

184
00:14:16.922 --> 00:14:22.922
As soon as you see a click clinic in the Christian world with TC, that is Teen Challenge.

185
00:14:22.922 --> 00:14:24.922
That comes from David Wilkerson.

186
00:14:24.922 --> 00:14:33.922
But the boss, the manager of branch 180TC, Sidney Troy Kiddo, came to me.

187
00:14:33.922 --> 00:14:38.922
While I was just telling that I was still broken and addicted.

188
00:14:38.922 --> 00:14:44.922
And Troy Kiddo came to me and said, I believe that the Lord has given me a mission to invite you.

189
00:14:44.922 --> 00:14:48.922
To come work at the addiction clinic.

190
00:14:48.922 --> 00:14:52.922
And I said to Troy Kiddo, dude, you don't even know who I am.

191
00:14:52.922 --> 00:14:55.922
Leave me alone. I should be in the program.

192
00:14:55.922 --> 00:14:59.922
Do you understand what I mean? I need to be in the program.

193
00:14:59.922 --> 00:15:02.922
I can't be a leader at all. How can I do that?

194
00:15:02.922 --> 00:15:08.922
And then Troy said, I am sure that I have heard God's voice.

195
00:15:08.922 --> 00:15:12.922
And God has selected you and I want to invite you no matter what.

196
00:15:12.922 --> 00:15:20.922
And for four years I was able to earn my bachelor's degree in Social Christian Works and Theology.

197
00:15:20.922 --> 00:15:28.922
And at the same time, I was able to work as an apprentice, that was the word I was looking for, at 180TC.

198
00:15:28.922 --> 00:15:30.922
And I learned so much there.

199
00:15:30.922 --> 00:15:34.922
I sometimes wonder where I learned more.

200
00:15:34.922 --> 00:15:37.922
In college or at 180TC.

201
00:15:37.922 --> 00:15:39.922
But the mix was amazing.

202
00:15:39.922 --> 00:15:44.922
God has set me free there and I am forever grateful to God.

203
00:15:44.922 --> 00:15:49.922
And sometimes when I read that Paul says I am a slave for Christ, I think to myself.

204
00:15:49.922 --> 00:15:56.922
Do you know that Jesus has bought you with His blood so that you are now the property of Christ?

205
00:15:56.922 --> 00:16:00.922
And if people take offense at what the Bible says about that.

206
00:16:00.922 --> 00:16:07.922
Then there is someone here who says I would rather be a slave of Christ than a slave of Satan.

207
00:16:07.922 --> 00:16:14.922
You are, after all, someone's property.

208
00:16:14.922 --> 00:16:18.922
Originally, you are the property of Abba Father in heaven.

209
00:16:18.922 --> 00:16:23.922
Through our free choices, we can detach ourselves from that, through disobedience.

210
00:16:23.922 --> 00:16:28.922
Then you connect yourself to the prince of the air, that is Satan in this world.

211
00:16:28.922 --> 00:16:31.922
He thinks he has ownership over many things.

212
00:16:31.922 --> 00:16:34.922
Because he can take people along in his lie.

213
00:16:34.922 --> 00:16:38.922
But I have been redeemed from that lie and I am now in Christ.

214
00:16:38.922 --> 00:16:47.922
One of the things I have been able to learn and I will explain to you these four weeks a few basic principles that I have learned.

215
00:16:47.922 --> 00:16:49.922
That I want to share with you.

216
00:16:49.922 --> 00:16:53.922
For those people who have studied psychology.

217
00:16:53.922 --> 00:16:56.922
Don't pick on me for the little things.

218
00:16:56.922 --> 00:17:00.922
So don't be legalistic with me.

219
00:17:00.922 --> 00:17:04.922
Because I am giving you the basic lessons of mine.

220
00:17:04.922 --> 00:17:11.922
Also in that theological training, we had one year of basics of psychology.

221
